onverted 2026-08-18 from a single 2026-10-15 gate)", "added_on": "2026-08-16", "review_id": "alert_rank_shadow_out_of_sample", "threshold": 1, "current_count": 23, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "RUNNING READ — fires again every session a new out-of-sample alert_date lands, from the first one. Every run: state n (COUNT(DISTINCT alert_date) WHERE alert_date > 2026-08-16) and its confidence label via `scripts/alert_rank_shadow_running_read.confidence_label` — n<25 is THIN/directional, NEVER presented as a verdict; n>=25 is DECISION-GRADE. Score catch-rate on the tail first (>=10R), medians second. Read the EOD version against the as-of-09:45 version separately (full-day tightness vs ORB-time-only — different questions). Report BOTH directions per quartile (winners admitted, losers admitted/excluded — see `score_both_directions`), never a winner count alone. Validates -> selection is actionable and the plan's sufficiency target stops depending entirely on conversion; does not -> the plan narrows to conversion alone.", "earliest_review_date": null, "last_resolution_date": "2026-10-09", "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}], "errored": [], "pending_count": 56, "pending_summary": [{"kind": "cadence", "title": "Chart reading — surface the next review sample for his ruling (#594)", "added_on": "2026-09-06", "review_id": "chart_reading_review_cycle", "threshold": 20, "blocked_by": "count=7 < threshold=20", "current_count": 7, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "🛑 OUTCOME-BLIND FROM SAMPLE #4 (his ruling 2026-10-10, \"go with rec\"): select both sides by\noutcome as below, but the PAGE he rules on shows NO forward return, NO \"it fell / it ran\" or\n\"alerted HIGH / skipped\" grouping, and the cards are SHUFFLED into one list. Every earlier\nverdict (sessions 1-4, 45 rulings) was given with a forward result on screen (5-day for session\n1, 20-day after), so agreement with outcomes measured nothing about his eye\n(docs/analysis/594_rulings_encoded_2026-10-10.md). Same day he ruled the $0 supply read a DEAD\nEND as a filter — do not re-score it after each sample; the labels now feed the three $0\nmeasures he cited and the bar #519's paid vision test must beat.\nBUILD THE NEXT SAMPLE, balanced both ways — never a list of failures:\n  A. names scored HIGH whose stock then collapsed (settled 20 sessions), and\n  B. names scored BELOW the bar whose stock then ran.\nTen total is what he engaged with; all dates must be settled at 20 sessions so\nnothing shown is still open.\n\nTHEN, in the same turn he replies:\n  1. Add every ruling to tests/fixtures/must_not_trade_charts.py keyed on\n     (ticker, DATE), with his words verbatim. Use GOOD_CHART / OKISH_CHART for\n     approvals — the vocabulary had NO positive label until 2026-09-06 and a file\n     that can only record rejections trains a filter that only knows how to reject.\n  2. Transcribe anything he shares into docs/methodology/ the SAME turn. Images are\n     saved to the repo AND transcribed; the 620 chart was lost by doing neither.\n  3. Re-check tests/test_577_must_not_miss_eps.py BEFORE anything else. The running\n     list of real EPs may never shrink.\n\n⚠ THE TRAP: with ~25 labelled dates and a free hand over five years of bars, a\nfavourable cutline is trivially findable and worthless. Any shape proposed from\nLOOKING must be declared in writing before it is measured, and measured on the TAIL\n(docs/methodology/analysis_standard.md § THE STATISTIC). The 2026-09-06 clearance\ntest is the worked example of doing this right: pre-declared, and it failed.", "earliest_review_date": "2026-09-20", "last_resolution_date": "2026-10-05", "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"kind": "tripwire", "title": "Re-cut the runner-exit sweep — on NEW TRADES or on a RULES CHANGE, whichever comes first", "added_on": null, "review_id": "runner_rule_sweep_recut", "threshold": 40, "blocked_by": "count=5 < threshold=40", "current_count": 5, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "RE-RUN THE SWEEP, do not re-derive it: scripts/probes/_bt_replay.py plus the Run-U\npopulation from docs/analysis/ep_backtest_run1_2026-08-29.md. It is a $0 query —\nan exit rule is arithmetic over bars we already store, so there is nothing to\nshadow and nothing to spend.\n\nWHICH ARM FIRED MATTERS:\n  - trade-count arm  -> the same question with a bigger n. Report whether any\n    rule now separates from the control at 95%, and whether the concentration in\n    a few correlated names has broken up.\n  - safeguard-change arm (each transition counts 40, so ONE fires it alone) ->\n    the prior read is STALE, not merely thin. Say which toggle moved and re-cut\n    the population under the new rules before comparing anything.\n\nREPORT: mean AND median per rule, n on every row, the win-rate cost, and the\nconcentration check. Then say plainly whether anything beats the control —\n\"the current rule is best\" is a real answer.\n\n⚖ THE LINE — exit discipline is the operator's. Evidence only; flip nothing.\n⚠ Blocked in practice by #605: while capture stays survivor-only the sample\ncannot improve honestly, so check #605 first.", "earliest_review_date": "2026-09-29", "last_resolution_date": null, "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"title": "Quarterly kill/scale band review (operator sign-off condition #1, 2026-06-12)", "review_id": "kill_scale_bands_quarterly_review", "blocked_by": "earliest_review_date=2026-11-26"}, {"kind": "accrual", "title": "The 2026-09-06 exit change has enough closed trades to read — did taking profit at +8R and moving the stop to breakeven at +3R improve what we KEEP?", "added_on": null, "review_id": "exit_rules_since_2026_09_06_first_readable_n", "threshold": 10, "blocked_by": "count=5 < threshold=10", "current_count": 5, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "Read the post-2026-09-06 closed magna53 live trades ALONE - never pooled with\nolder ones. Report kept-vs-peak, win rate, expectancy in R and stop-out share,\neach with its n, and say how many had an unreadable peak (the <10m recorder\nblind spot) rather than counting those as zero capture.\n⚖ REPORTS ONLY. An exit change is entry/exit discipline - CHANGE_PROCESS,\nN>=10 backtest and operator sign-off before anything moves (THE LINE).", "earliest_review_date": "2026-09-20", "last_resolution_date": null, "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"kind": "accrual", "title": "The 50-75% extension band now holds 94 scoreable names (bar was 15) — does it carry edge, or is the STOP still the binding constraint?", "added_on": null, "review_id": "extension_cap_75_recheck", "threshold": 15, "blocked_by": "count=7 < threshold=15", "current_count": 7, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "⚠ Read the band as it stands under the LIVE 50% cap — NOT as \"names the\n75% raise admitted\", which is a population that stopped existing on\n2026-08-29. Replay the 94 scoreable names through the live bracket on\nminute bars (the method of docs/analysis/577_extension_cap_recheck_2026-08-29.md,\nso the two reads are comparable), filtered on last_refreshed_at (the #583\nstale-row class). Report: did the admitted band produce winners, and\ndo the names still being skipped carry the +58%-average tail the 08-23\nreview showed? ⚖ The cap is entry discipline — THE LINE. This review\nREPORTS; any further change needs CHANGE_PROCESS + operator sign-off.", "earliest_review_date": "2026-09-15", "last_resolution_date": "2026-09-21", "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}]}, "postmortem_best": {"pnl": -58.95, "ticker": "CEG", "narrative": "📋 *Postmortem — CEG 2026-10-06*\n\n*Setup*\nThe alert was legitimate but marginal. The Google 890 MW offtake is a real, company-specific catalyst, but Gemini and Claude both graded it only \"strong\". The deal is small against a $94.8B market cap and follows the Amazon deal, so part of it was already priced in. EP 65 sat exactly on the Choppy-regime bar of 65, so it cleared with no cushion. Breadth was weak (T2108 30%, 29.6% above the 40MA). Theme context helped: the IPP/nuclear group had RS 89.8, but both themes were only \"Nascent\". Relative volume of 0.13 and a 0th volume percentile gave no confirmation at trigger.\n\n*Execution*\nThe entry was clean. It filled on the first attempt at `300.94`, about a minute after the open and just above the ORB high of `300.71`. The stop at `281.29` was about 1.9 ATR away, below the ORB low, and risk came in at `$58` against `$77` planned. The partial never fired because the high of `309.80` was only about +2.9% from entry. The broker-side dead stop shows `EXPIRED` and `stop_order_id` is null, so the position had no resting broker stop after day one. The exit came from the websocket software stop at 16:52 UTC on 10/08. It is recorded at exactly `281.29`, but the intraday low of `281.06` suggests real slippage may differ from the log.\n\n*Outcome*\nThe trade lost `-$58.95`, about -1R on actual risk. Price ran to `309.80` and faded. The day-1 close of `299.59` was below entry, consistent with the forward 1d return of -0.27%. It then broke the stop two sessions later. The 1w, 1m and SPY comparisons are not available yet, so I can't judge follow-through beyond that. The stop did its job, but the setup never showed momentum.\n\n*Lesson*\nSkip at-the-bar EP scores on partly priced catalysts in Choppy regimes unless volume confirms, and make the broker-side stop GTC so it doesn't expire and leave the position relying on the websocket.", "alert_date": "2026-10-06"}, "postmortem_worst": null, "n