 2026-09-29T21:03:12.066960+00:00"}, {"rule": "quiet: it has not recurred in 4d (Tue 09-29 17:03 ET)", "what": "theme_parent_pass_error at 2026-09-29T21:03:14.620707+00:00"}, {"rule": "quiet: it has not recurred in 4d (Tue 09-29 17:03 ET)", "what": "theme_parent_pass_error at 2026-09-29T21:03:18.287433+00:00"}, {"rule": "quiet: it has not recurred in 4d (Tue 09-29 18:05 ET)", "what": "theme_synthesis_error at 2026-09-29T22:05:10.872051+00:00"}, {"rule": "quiet: it has not recurred in 4d (Tue 09-29 18:00 ET)", "what": "crypto_ingest_error at 2026-09-29T22:00:00.138254+00:00"}, {"rule": "quiet: StructuredOutputError has not recurred in 4d (Tue 09-29 17:01 ET)", "what": "assignment_error at 2026-09-29T21:01:46.469495+00:00"}, {"rule": "quiet: it has not recurred in 6d (Mon 09-28 07:00 ET)", "what": "judge_divergence_check_failed at 2026-09-28T11:00:33.019882+00:00"}]}, "judge_weekly": {"total": 3, "judged": 3, "demotes": 0, "no_fire": 0, "promotes": 0, "fallbacks": 0, "fire_seen": 3, "window_days": 7, "judge_driven": 3}, "paper_trades": {"best": null, "worst": null, "win_rate": null, "avg_pnl_pct": null, "total_closed": 0}, "loser_breakdown": {}, "nine_m_outcomes": {"green": 0, "total": 0, "win_rate": null, "with_outcome": 0, "avg_fwd_1w_pct": null}, "pending_reviews": {"ready": [{"kind": "accrual", "title": "Catalyst-discovery loop (investigator + advisor) — C2/C3 build sequencing gate (ADR 0006)", "added_on": "2026-05-30", "review_id": "catalyst_discovery_loop_sequencing", "threshold": 30, "current_count": 210, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": true}, "action_when_ready": "Build per ADR 0006 §7 smallest-viable sequence: (1) cohort accessor + RS-slope filter\n(reuse correlation_engine + mi_stock_scores rs_1m/rs_6m), (2) rung-1 investigator on a\nSINGLE case, (3) rung-1.5 advisor pass (Sonnet critique + bounded revise), (4) nightly\njob + mi_catalyst_dossiers + Telegram surface (advisory/shadow). ACCEPTANCE TEST =\nreproduce the drones + software-AI cohorts read-only (ADR 0006 §6) — that IS the proof\nof capability the operator asked for. Advisor + go-live sequencing review BEFORE any\ncode. Cross-ref ADR 0006, theme_engine_narrative_blindness, theme_as_ep_signal.", "earliest_review_date": "2026-10-01", "last_resolution_date": null, "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"kind": "accrual", "title": "L2 baseline window too sluggish for trending metrics (earnings-season transitions)", "added_on": "2026-05-20", "review_id": "l2_baseline_window_trending_metrics", "threshold": 6, "current_count": 47, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": true}, "action_when_ready": "With ≥6 L2 events in last 90d, categorize each:\n  - FP (false positive, metric in transition): supports change\n  - TP (real anomaly correctly surfaced): cautions against\n      window change\n\nIf ≥4 of 6 are FPs from trending-metric class:\n  Phase 1 — Telemetry-only ship: tag each L2 with a `trending`\n    classifier (monotonic-3-of-5d?, regression slope?) and emit\n    an audit event for FP-likely L2s. Keep firing the alert but\n    downgrade the framing. 30d telemetry.\n  Phase 2 — Threshold change: shift to EWMA OR shorter window\n    for metrics flagged trending, based on cohort outcomes.\n\nIf <4 of 6 are FPs: keep current 30d window. The L2 sensitivity\nis doing its job.\n\nCross-reference: silent_failure_taxonomy_audit (this is the\nobservability-class case: alarm fires but signal is noise).", "earliest_review_date": "2026-10-01", "last_resolution_date": null, "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"kind": "accrual", "title": "Steady-state cost of theme assignment after the 08-10 output-bounding fix — does the backlog cost decay, and did batch=18 hold?", "added_on": "2026-08-10", "review_id": "theme_assignment_steady_state_cost", "threshold": 5, "current_count": 37, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "Report cost/night and uncovered-pool size/night AS A PAIR (cost alone is uninterpretable — it is ~73 output tokens per unassigned stock, so it must be read against the pool), plus the trend and implied monthly run-rate. THEN the value side, or the cost means nothing: average theme membership and the count of themes holding <=3 tickers, against the 2026-08-10 baseline of 460 theme rows / avg 3.3 members / 350 of 460 at <=3. Three outcomes: (a) cost decays and membership rises => keep, report the floor; (b) cost flat and membership rises => real ongoing price for a working component, operator rules; (c) membership does NOT rise => the spend bought nothing, pull it. ALSO: if `theme_assignment` still shows stop_reason='max_tokens' rows, batch=18 was modelled too high (no untruncated sonnet-5 sample existed to measure it) — halve it.", "earliest_review_date": "2026-10-01", "last_resolution_date": null, "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"kind": "accrual", "title": "Ranking rule — RUNNING out-of-sample read (converted 2026-08-18 from a single 2026-10-15 gate)", "added_on": "2026-08-16", "review_id": "alert_rank_shadow_out_of_sample", "threshold": 1, "current_count": 18, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "RUNNING READ — fires again every session a new out-of-sample alert_date lands, from the first one. Every run: state n (COUNT(DISTINCT alert_date) WHERE alert_date > 2026-08-16) and its confidence label via `scripts/alert_rank_shadow_running_read.confidence_label` — n<25 is THIN/directional, NEVER presented as a verdict; n>=25 is DECISION-GRADE. Score catch-rate on the tail first (>=10R), medians second. Read the EOD version against the as-of-09:45 version separately (full-day tightness vs ORB-time-only — different questions). Report BOTH directions per quartile (winners admitted, losers admitted/excluded — see `score_both_directions`), never a winner count alone. Validates -> selection is actionable and the plan's sufficiency target stops depending entirely on conversion; does not -> the plan narrows to conversion alone.", "earliest_review_date": null, "last_resolution_date": "2026-10-02", "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}], "errored": [], "pending_count": 54, "pending_summary": [{"kind": "cadence", "title": "Chart reading — surface the next review sample for his ruling (#594)", "added_on": "2026-09-06", "review_id": "chart_reading_review_cycle", "threshold": 20, "blocked_by": "count=18 < threshold=20", "current_count": 18, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "BUILD THE NEXT SAMPLE, balanced both ways — never a list of failures:\n  A. names scored HIGH whose stock then collapsed (settled 20 sessions), and\n  B. names scored BELOW the bar whose stock then ran.\nTen total is what he engaged with; all dates must be settled at 20 sessions so\nnothing shown is still open.\n\nTHEN, in the same turn he replies:\n  1. Add every ruling to tests/fixtures/must_not_trade_charts.py keyed on\n     (ticker, DATE), with his words verbatim. Use GOOD_CHART / OKISH_CHART for\n     approvals — the vocabulary had NO positive label until 2026-09-06 and a file\n     that can only record rejections trains a filter that only knows how to reject.\n  2. Transcribe anything he shares into docs/methodology/ the SAME turn. Images are\n     saved to the repo AND transcribed; the 620 chart was lost by doing neither.\n  3. Re-check tests/test_577_must_not_miss_eps.py BEFORE anything else. The running\n     list of real EPs may never shrink.\n\n⚠ THE TRAP: with ~25 labelled dates and a free hand over five years of bars, a\nfavourable cutline is trivially findable and worthless. Any shape proposed from\nLOOKING must be declared in writing before it is measured, and measured on the TAIL\n(docs/methodology/analysis_standard.md § THE STATISTIC). The 2026-09-06 clearance\ntest is the worked example of doing this right: pre-declared, and it failed.", "earliest_review_date": "2026-09-20", "last_resolution_date": null, "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"kind": "tripwire", "title": "Re-cut the runner-exit sweep — on NEW TRADES or on a RULES CHANGE, whichever comes first", "added_on": null, "review_id": "runner_rule_sweep_recut", "threshold": 40, "blocked_by": "count=3 < threshold=40", "current_count": 3, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "RE-RUN THE SWEEP, do not re-derive it: scripts/probes/_bt_replay.py plus the Run-U\npopulation from docs/analysis/ep_backtest_run1_2026-08-29.md. It is a $0 query —\nan exit rule is arithmetic over bars we already store, so there is nothing to\nshadow and nothing to spend.\n\nWHICH ARM FIRED MATTERS:\n  - trade-count arm  -> the same question with a bigger n. Report whether any\n    rule now separates from the control at 95%, and whether the concentration in\n    a few correlated names has broken up.\n  - safeguard-change arm (each transition counts 40, so ONE fires it alone) ->\n    the prior read is STALE, not merely thin. Say which toggle moved and re-cut\n    the population under the new rules before comparing anything.\n\nREPORT: mean AND median per rule, n on every row, the win-rate cost, and the\nconcentration check. Then say plainly whether anything beats the control —\n\"the current rule is best\" is a real answer.\n\n⚖ THE LINE — exit discipline is the operator's. Evidence only; flip nothing.\n⚠ Blocked in practice by #605: while capture stays survivor-only the sample\ncannot improve honestly, so check #605 first.", "earliest_review_date": "2026-09-29", "last_resolution_date": null, "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"title": "Quarterly kill/scale band review (operator sign-off condition #1, 2026-06-12)", "review_id": "kill_scale_bands_quarterly_review", "blocked_by": "earliest_review_date=2026-11-26"}, {"kind": "accrual", "title": "The 2026-09-06 exit change has enough closed trades to read — did taking profit at +8R and moving the stop to breakeven at +3R improve what we KEEP?", "added_on": null, "review_id": "exit_rules_since_2026_09_06_first_readable_n", "threshold": 10, "blocked_by": "count=3 < threshold=10", "current_count": 3, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "Read the post-2026-09-06 closed magna53 live trades ALONE - never pooled with\nolder ones. Report kept-vs-peak, win rate, expectancy in R and stop-out share,\neach with its n, and say how many had an unreadable peak (the <10m recorder\nblind spot) rather than counting those as zero capture.\n⚖ REPORTS ONLY. An exit change is entry/exit discipline - CHANGE_PROCESS,\nN>=10 backtest and operator sign-off before anything moves (THE LINE).", "earliest_review_date": "2026-09-20", "last_resolution_date": null, "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"kind": "accrual", "title": "The 50-75% extension band now holds 94 scoreable names (bar was 15) — does it carry edge, or is the STOP still the binding constraint?", "added_on": null, "review_id": "extension_cap_75_recheck", "threshold": 15, "blocked_by": "count=6 < threshold=15", "current_count": 6, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "⚠ Read the band as it stands under the LIVE 50% cap — NOT as \"names the\n75% raise admitted\", which is a population that stopped existing on\n2026-08-29. Replay the 94 scoreable names through the live bracket on\nminute bars (the method of docs/analysis/577_extension_cap_recheck_2026-08-29.md,\nso the two reads are comparable), filtered on last_refreshed_at (the #583\nstale-row class). Report: did the admitted band produce winners, and\ndo the names still being skipped carry the +58%-average tail the 08-23\nreview showed? ⚖ The cap is entry discipline — THE LINE. This review\nREPORTS; any further change needs CHANGE_PROCESS + operator sign-off.", "earliest_review_date": "2026-09-15", "last_resolution_date": "2026-09-21", "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}]}, "postmortem_best": null, "postmortem_worst": null, "news_source_quality": {"drift_events": [], "current_stats": {"Polygon": {"coverage_pct": 66.7, "n_extractions": 3, "coverage_count": 2, "density_median": 3, "attribution_pct": 0.0, "attribution_count": 0}, "Perplexity": {"coverage_pct": 100.0, "n_extractions": 3, "coverage_count": 3, "density_median": 544, "attribution_pct": 33.3, "attribution_count": 1}, "Alpaca/Benzinga": {"coverage_pct": 100.0, "n_extractions": 3, "coverage_count": 3, "density_median": 14, "attribution_pct": 100.0, "attribution_count": 3}, "Claude analysis": {"coverage_pct": 100.0, "n_extractions": 3, "coverage_count": 3, "density_median": 413, "attribution_pct": 100.0, "attribution_count": 3}, "yfinance (legacy 'fmp')": {"coverage_pct": 0.0, "n_extractions": 3, "coverage_count": 0, "density_median": 0, "attribution_pct": 0.0, "attribution_count": 0}}, "current_window": "2026-09-28..2026-10-04", "baseline_window": "2026-09-05..2026-09-27"}, "strategy_promotions": {"checks": [{"model": "telemetry_review", "metrics": {"fill_rate": 0.635, "n_candidates": 52}, "eligible": false, "next_phase": "paper", "strategy_id": "wick_fill", "current_phase": "shadow", "blocking_reasons": ["manual review fields not yet captured — eligibility deferred"]}, {"model": "unpaired_r", "metrics": {}, "eligible": false, "next_phase": null, "strategy_id": "9m_day2", "current_phase": "deprecated", "blocking_reasons": ["deprecated — excluded from promotion ladder"]}, {"model": "telemetry_review", "metrics": {}, "eligible": false, "next_phase": null, "strategy_id": "flag_continuation", "current_phase": "deprec