READ — fires again every session a new out-of-sample alert_date lands, from the first one. Every run: state n (COUNT(DISTINCT alert_date) WHERE alert_date > 2026-08-16) and its confidence label via `scripts/alert_rank_shadow_running_read.confidence_label` — n<25 is THIN/directional, NEVER presented as a verdict; n>=25 is DECISION-GRADE. Score catch-rate on the tail first (>=10R), medians second. Read the EOD version against the as-of-09:45 version separately (full-day tightness vs ORB-time-only — different questions). Report BOTH directions per quartile (winners admitted, losers admitted/excluded — see `score_both_directions`), never a winner count alone. Validates -> selection is actionable and the plan's sufficiency target stops depending entirely on conversion; does not -> the plan narrows to conversion alone.", "earliest_review_date": null, "last_resolution_date": "2026-09-26", "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}], "errored": [], "pending_count": 55, "pending_summary": [{"kind": "cadence", "title": "Chart reading — surface the next review sample for his ruling (#594)", "added_on": "2026-09-06", "review_id": "chart_reading_review_cycle", "threshold": 20, "blocked_by": "count=15 < threshold=20", "current_count": 15, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "BUILD THE NEXT SAMPLE, balanced both ways — never a list of failures:\n  A. names scored HIGH whose stock then collapsed (settled 20 sessions), and\n  B. names scored BELOW the bar whose stock then ran.\nTen total is what he engaged with; all dates must be settled at 20 sessions so\nnothing shown is still open.\n\nTHEN, in the same turn he replies:\n  1. Add every ruling to tests/fixtures/must_not_trade_charts.py keyed on\n     (ticker, DATE), with his words verbatim. Use GOOD_CHART / OKISH_CHART for\n     approvals — the vocabulary had NO positive label until 2026-09-06 and a file\n     that can only record rejections trains a filter that only knows how to reject.\n  2. Transcribe anything he shares into docs/methodology/ the SAME turn. Images are\n     saved to the repo AND transcribed; the 620 chart was lost by doing neither.\n  3. Re-check tests/test_577_must_not_miss_eps.py BEFORE anything else. The running\n     list of real EPs may never shrink.\n\n⚠ THE TRAP: with ~25 labelled dates and a free hand over five years of bars, a\nfavourable cutline is trivially findable and worthless. Any shape proposed from\nLOOKING must be declared in writing before it is measured, and measured on the TAIL\n(docs/methodology/analysis_standard.md § THE STATISTIC). The 2026-09-06 clearance\ntest is the worked example of doing this right: pre-declared, and it failed.", "earliest_review_date": "2026-09-20", "last_resolution_date": null, "last_run_inconclusive_on": null}, {"title": "Re-cut the runner-exit sweep — on NEW TRADES or on a RULES CHANGE, whichever comes first", "review_id": "runner_rule_sweep_recut", "blocked_by": "earliest_review_date=2026-09-29"}, {"title": "Quarterly kill/scale band review (operator sign-off condition #1, 2026-06-12)", "review_id": "kill_scale_bands_quarterly_review", "blocked_by": "earliest_review_date=2026-11-26"}, {"kind": "accrual", "title": "The 2026-09-06 exit change has enough closed trades to read — did taking profit at +8R and moving the stop to breakeven at +3R improve what we KEEP?", "added_on": null, "review_id": "exit_rules_since_2026_09_06_first_readable_n", "threshold": 10, "blocked_by": "count=3 < threshold=10", "current_count": 3, "last_run_note": null, "evidence_flags": {"date_fire": false, "population_mismatch": [], "population_undeclared": false}, "action_when_ready": "Read the post-2026-09-06 closed magna53 live trades ALONE - never pooled with\nolder ones. Report kept-vs-peak, win rate, expectancy in R and stop-out share,\neach with its n, and say how many had an unreadable peak (the <10m recorder\nblind spot) rather than counting those 